---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Help"
  description="Answers to common questions about reading, navigating, and getting the most out of The Lunan."
>
  <main class="pt-[64px]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-4 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24">
      <!-- Pill badge -->
      <span
        class="font-manrope mb-6 inline-block rounded-full bg-[#ebf3ed] px-3 py-1 text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[3px] text-[#386547] uppercase"
      >
        Help
      </span>

      <!-- Heading -->
      <h1
        class="font-space-grotesk text-[38px] leading-[1.05] font-bold tracking-[-0.04em] text-[#29302d] sm:text-[46px] md:text-[52px]"
      >
        How this place works
      </h1>

      <!-- Divider -->
      <div class="my-6 h-[2px] w-10 rounded-full bg-[#c5f7d0]"></div>

      <p
        class="font-manrope mb-10 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.65)]"
      >
        The Lunan is a personal blog. No algorithm, no feed, no notifications.
        Here&apos;s how to find your way around.
      </p>

      <!-- Body -->
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-space-grotesk mt-4 mb-3 text-[20px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[#29302d]"
          >
            Reading posts
          </h2>
          <p
            class="font-manrope text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.65)]"
          >
            The home page shows the latest writing. Click any title to open the
            full post. At the bottom of each post you&apos;ll find a clap button
            (like a like, but better), share links, a comment section, and a few
            related posts to keep reading.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-space-grotesk mt-4 mb-3 text-[20px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[#29302d]"
          >
            Archive
          </h2>
          <p
            class="font-manrope text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.65)]"
          >
            The <a
              href="/archive"
              class="font-semibold text-[#386547] hover:underline">Archive</a
            > lists every post in one place, sorted by date. It&apos;s the best place
            to catch up if you&apos;re new here.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-space-grotesk mt-4 mb-3 text-[20px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[#29302d]"
          >
            Topics
          </h2>
          <p
            class="font-manrope text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.65)]"
          >
            Posts are tagged by topic. Visit <a
              href="/topics"
              class="font-semibold text-[#386547] hover:underline">Topics</a
            > to browse everything by category &mdash; useful if you only want to
            read about a specific thing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-space-grotesk mt-4 mb-3 text-[20px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[#29302d]"
          >
            Search
          </h2>
          <p
            class="font-manrope text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.65)]"
          >
            Hit the search icon in the top-right of the navbar (or press
            <kbd
              class="rounded-[4px] border border-[rgba(41,48,45,0.15)] bg-white px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[12px] text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.6)]"
              >/</kbd
            > on your keyboard) to search across all posts by title, description,
            or tag.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-space-grotesk mt-4 mb-3 text-[20px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[#29302d]"
          >
            RSS feed
          </h2>
          <p
            class="font-manrope text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.65)]"
          >
            Prefer a feed reader? Subscribe via <a
              href="/rss.xml"
              class="font-semibold text-[#386547] hover:underline">RSS</a
            >. Every new post shows up there automatically, no account needed.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-space-grotesk mt-4 mb-3 text-[20px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[#29302d]"
          >
            Comments
          </h2>
          <p
            class="font-manrope text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.65)]"
          >
            Each post has a comment section at the bottom. Comments are
            anonymous &mdash; no account, no email, just type and post. You can
            reply to any comment once. Keep it kind.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2
            class="font-space-grotesk mt-4 mb-3 text-[20px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[#29302d]"
          >
            Something broken?
          </h2>
          <p
            class="font-manrope text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.65)]"
          >
            If a page isn&apos;t loading, a link is dead, or something looks
            wrong, drop a comment on any post and I&apos;ll take a look. This
            site is a side project built from scratch &mdash; bugs happen.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Footer nav -->
      <div class="mt-14 border-t border-[rgba(197,247,208,0.4)] pt-8">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="font-manrope group inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold text-[rgba(41,48,45,0.5)] transition-colors hover:text-[#386547]"
        >
          <svg
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 14 14"
            fill="none"
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5"
          >
            <path
              d="M13 7H1M6 2L1 7l5 5"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.5"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          </svg>
          Back home
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
